SUMMARY:🍽️ Book the Europe restaurant tables
DESCRIPTION:Every timed ticket and both shows are now BOOKED. What's left is restaurants:\n• The Brazen Head dinner Fri Nov 13 — book 7:30 PM so dinner runs into the ~9:30 trad session\n• The Delaunay dinner Sun Nov 15 (thedelaunay.com)\n• Westminster Abbey ~12:15 Mon Nov 16 — NOV NOT LOADED YET (only to Oct 31 as of Sep 6). Separate reminder starts Sep 20.\n• [DONE] London Eye — booked, Mon 16 Nov 3:30 PM, Fast Track x2, order 123678423\n• Gillray's dinner Mon Nov 16 (reserve a river-view table)\n• Tue Nov 17 dinner: ROYAL CHINA CHINATOWN, 30 Gerrard St -- book 5:30, say "7 o'clock show at the Palace". WOULDN'T TAKE NOV 17 ON SEP 6 (too far out), so retry from late Sept. !! CONFIRM THE ADDRESS IS 30 GERRARD STREET -- their booking widget defaults to Harrow-on-the-Hill, 40 min away in Zone 5. Direct line +44 20 7734 1388. Also ask if dim sum is still served at 5:30. If it never opens up, just walk in -- Chinatown on a Nov Tuesday is fine, and it's 4 min from your seats.\n• [DONE] Cursed Child — booked, Tue 17 Nov 7:00 PM, Palace Theatre, Dress Circle A19+A20, GBP 250\n• [DONE] Tower of London — booked, Wed 18 Nov (all-day ticket), order DVOMY243MYHM2\n• Café Murano pre-theatre dinner Wed Nov 18 ~5:45 (reserve)\n• [DONE] Phantom of the Opera — booked, Wed 18 Nov 7:30 PM, Royal Circle A19+A20, GBP 370\n• Rules dinner Thu Nov 19 — London farewell (rules.co.uk, reserve ahead)\n• Chez Georges (first Paris dinner) Fri Nov 20 — reserve if you want a sit-down bistro (or Bouillon Chartier walk-in)\n• Le Grand Colbert dinner Sat Nov 21 — reserve (legrandcolbert.fr)\n• Sainte-Chapelle ~12:15 Sun Nov 22 — NOV NOT LOADED YET (only to Oct 31 as of Sep 6). Separate reminder starts Sep 25.\n• Notre-Dame free slot — reserve ~2 days ahead DURING the trip (app/site)\n• Chez Janou dinner Sun Nov 22 — reserve (chezjanou.com)\n• [DONE] Musee d'Orsay — booked, Tue 24 Nov 9:30 AM, transaction 200696183\n• La Bonne Franquette (last Paris dinner) Tue Nov 24 — reserve (or Bouillon Pigalle walk-in)\nMOST OF THESE WILL BE TOO FAR OUT UNTIL OCTOBER -- London/Paris restaurants typically open 30-60 days ahead. Confirmed on Sep 6: Royal China Chinatown would not take Nov 17. So work this list again in early October; nothing here is lost by waiting, and every one of them has a walk-in fallback.\n\nDONE so far: Book of Kells - Louvre - Tower of London - London Eye - Musee d'Orsay - Phantom - Cursed Child. ALL TIMED TICKETS AND BOTH SHOWS ARE BOOKED. What's left here is restaurants only.\n\n--\nTHIS REMINDER REPEATS EVERY WEEK until its deadline. Subscribed calendars are read-only, so iOS won't offer Snooze -- just dismiss it and it will come back. Once you've actually done this one, tell Claude and it gets removed from the feed for good.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Book the Europe restaurant tables  (repeats until done)
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
