SUMMARY:🛂 UK ETA - BOTH of you, before you can board (£20 each)
DESCRIPTION:BOTH OF YOU NEED THIS -- it is a boarding requirement, not a formality. Since 25 Feb 2026 US citizens must hold an approved UK Electronic Travel Authorisation before boarding a flight to the UK. You fly Dublin-London on BA on Sun 15 Nov.\n\nThe Common Travel Area exemption does NOT cover you: it applies to Irish citizens and lawful residents of Ireland, not Americans visiting. Airlines check documents before boarding even on Ireland-UK routes, so BA will look for it at Dublin.\n\nHOW: gov.uk/eta or the official UK ETA app. GBP 20 each (about USD 25), valid 2 years, usually approved in minutes. !! Apply ONLY through those two -- third-party sites charge a big markup for the identical thing.\n\nWHILE YOU HAVE BOTH PASSPORTS OUT, check two things:\n1. EXPIRY -- France needs them valid until at least 25 FEB 2027 (3 months past your 25 Nov departure).\n2. ISSUE DATE -- Schengen also requires the passport was ISSUED WITHIN THE LAST 10 YEARS, so issued after ~25 NOV 2016. An older passport that hasn't expired can still be refused. If either fails, renew NOW, not in October.\n\n(ETIAS for Europe is NOT required -- it has not launched and 2027 is now the likely date. Anyone selling you one is scamming you.)\n\n--\nTHIS REMINDER REPEATS EVERY 2 DAYS until done. Tell Claude once it's approved and it comes out of the feed.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Apply for the UK ETA - gov.uk/eta, both passports, GBP 20 each  (repeats until done)
TRIGGER:PT0S
END:VALARM
